QuestGuidance.Register("en",211,{
[6721]="70002E86\n1\tTalk to Severin Wheeler\tSeverin Wheeler is standing by the Trestlebridge. Severin Wheeler is waiting to assign you your position in the defence of the town.\n2\tSeverin Wheeler told you that several men have come to aid in the defence of Trestlebridge. Before he left to aid a group of farmers trapped in the North Downs, Severin Wheeler charged you with keeping any marauding Orcs away from the bridge. You should speak with the men nearby to assign them their positions.\t\n3\tTalk to defenders of Trestlebridge\tHilton Harper is standing in front of the Trestlespan. Hilton Harper is waiting to speak with you about organizing the defence of Trestlebridge.\n4\tTalk to Hilton Harper\tHilton Harper is outside Trestlebridge. Hilton Harper is waiting to speak with you about your defence of the town.\n",
[6722]="7003FE89\n1\tOffer to help Limril with dinner while she waits for Fuirion to arrive\tLimril is in her home in Dínadab in northern Lamedon. You should offer to help Limril with dinner while she waits for Fuirion.\n2\tGather dishes from the hutch\tThe hutch is in the corner. You should gather dishes from the hutch, and set the table.\n3\tSet the table for six (total: 6)\tThe table is in Gladion and Limril's home. You should gather dishes from the hutch, and set the table.\n4\tTalk to Limril\tLimril is in her home in Dínadab in northern Lamedon. You should see what else Limril needs.\n5\tFind out what the commotion is all about\tGladion kneels at the door with his brother in his arms. You should ask Gladion what happened to his brother Fuirion.\n6\tExamine Fuirion\tFuirion is at Gladion's doorstep. You should examine Fuirion.\n",
[6723]="70049564\n1\tTalk to Gimli\tGimli is standing in Lûghash. King Greytooth has asked you and Gimli to share your tales of valour with him and his folk that he might learn of the path that led you to Mordor.\n2\tFollow Gimli and join King Greytooth among the Stout-axes of Lûghash\tKing Greytooth is eager to hear tales of valour from you and Gimli. You should not keep him waiting.\n3\tTell King Greytooth the story of the Ring-bearer's quest\tKing Greytooth is standing in Lûghash. You should tell him of your many tales of valour, especially those you shared with Gimli.\n4\tTell King Greytooth the story of the battles of the Hornburg and of the Pelennor Fields\tKing Greytooth is standing in Lûghash. You should tell him of your many tales of valour, especially those you shared with Gimli.\n5\tTell King Greytooth the story of Skorgrím and of the lost Dwarf-kingdom of Khazad-dûm\tKing Greytooth is standing in Lûghash. You should tell him of your many tales of valour, especially those you shared with Gimli.\n6\tListen to Gimli tell the tale of Smaug and the Battle of Five Armies\tGimli is addressing King Greytooth in Lûghash. You should listen to his tale.\n7\tWitness Sversting present his tribute to King Greytooth\tSversting, the master-smith of Lûghash, has crafted a keen axe for King Greytooth and now wishes to present it to him.\n8\tFollow King Greytooth and learn of his secret\tSpakorth has noticed a peculiar key upon a necklace worn by King Greytooth. King Greytooth is willing to speak of it, but wishes to do so privately.\n9\tDefeat the fell spirit that was inhabiting Spakorth\tSpakorth attempted to steal the key from King Greytooth, and after being thwarted, a fell spirit has risen from him. Spakorth lies wounded, but the fell spirit appears unharmed.\n10\tTalk to King Greytooth\tKing Greytooth is standing above the defeated Spakorth. You should speak to him and learn what is to be done.\n11\tTalk to King Greytooth\tYou have come to Zôreth's chamber with King Greytooth and the Stout-axes. You should now speak to him and confront the Mistress of Lûghash.\n12\tConfront Zôreth\tZôreth is standing in her chamber. You should join King Greytooth and the Stout-axes in confronting her and putting an end to her treachery.\n13\tTalk to King Greytooth\tKing Greytooth is standing in Zôreth's chamber in Lûghash. Despite freeing his people from the Mistress of Lûghash, King Greytooth appears more troubled than ever. You should speak to him.\n",
[6724]="700010A0\n1\tTalk to Gytha Lainey\tGytha Lainey is on the road outside Overhill. You have come to Overhill with Gytha Lainey to save its people from the danger that threatens them. Gytha is waiting to speak with you about how to proceed.\n2\tTalk to Gammer Boffin\030Talk to Hart Holeman\030Talk to Otho Broadbelt\030Talk to Postman Boffin\tThe people of Overhill are going about their business, oblivious to the danger that lurks somewhere north of their town. Gytha has told you to warn the people of Overhill to stay inside their houses until the danger has passed.\n3\tTalk to Gytha Lainey\tGytha Lainey is in the town of Overhill. Now that you have told the people of Overhill to go inside their houses, it is up to you and Gytha to stop the intruding Wargs.\n4\tTalk to Gytha Lainey\tGytha Lainey is in Overhill. You have successfully defeated the Warg hunting-party that intruded into the Bindbole Wood and should now speak of your success to Gytha Lainey.\n",
[6725]="7006F399\n1\tTalk to Rahâzi inside the waggon\tRahâzi is hidden inside the waggon.\n2\tListen for anyone who might approach\030Stand near the back of the waggon\tYou should stand near the back of the waggon and listen for anyone to approach too near.\n3\tTry not to move or make any noise\tDo not move, and make no noise!\n4\tTalk to Rahâzi inside the waggon\tRahâzi is hidden inside the waggon.\n5\tPass the time while the waggon rumbles to its destination\tIt will be some time before the waggon arrives. Now you can only wait.\n6\tTalk to Rahâzi inside the waggon\tRahâzi is hidden inside the waggon.\n7\tListen for anyone who might approach\030Stand near the back of the waggon\tYou should stand near the back of the waggon and listen for anyone to approach too near.\n8\tWait for the driver to leave before departing the waggon\tIf the driver moves away, it should be safe to depart the waggon.\n",
[6726]="7002FA17\n1\tTalk to Corudan\tCorudan is waiting to speak with you beside the river where you have stopped for the night.\n2\tTalk to Horn by the camp-fire\030Talk to Nona by the camp-fire\tHorn and Nona are sitting on opposite sides of the camp-fire by the Anduin.\n3\tTalk to Corudan by the camp-fire\tCorudan is sitting by the camp-fire.\n4\tTalk to Corudan and decide upon a tale to share\tCorudan is sitting by the camp-fire.\n5\tTalk to Horn by the camp-fire\tHorn is sitting by the fire.\n6\tListen to Horn's story\tListen to Horn tell his story of King Fengel.\n7\tTalk to Horn by the camp-fire\tHorn is waiting to finish the story of King Fengel and Wyrgende the crone.\n8\tTalk to Nona by the camp-fire\tNona is sitting by the camp-fire, waiting to tell her story.\n9\tListen to Nona's story\tNona is telling a story by the camp-fire.\n10\tTalk to Corudan by the camp-fire\tCorudan is by the camp-fire, waiting to speak with you.\n",
[6727]="70041357\n1\tSpeak with Erchar\tErchar and Herion meet at the battleground. You should speak to Erchar.\n2\tListen to the conversation between Erchar and Herion.\tErchar and Herion meet at the battleground. You should listen to the conversation between Erchar and Herion.\n3\tKneel before the brave warrior to pay your respects\030Covered fallen warriors in soil (total: 5)\tThe bodies of Gondorian warriors slain by the Corsair forces can be found at the battleground. You should cover the bodies with soil and pay your respects.\n4\tSpeak with Herion\tHerion is at the battleground. You should speak with Herion.\n5\tSpeak with Erchar\tErchar is at the battleground. You should speak with Erchar.\n",
[6728]="700645A8\n1\tTalk to Glindor in the Tower of Ecthelion\tGlindor has brought you to the Tower of Ecthelion, where King Elessar and Queen Arwen await you.\n2\tTalk to King Elessar in the Tower of Ecthelion\tKing Elessar is ready to speak with you about his plans.\n3\tListen to the discussion of King Elessar's plans\tKing Elessar and his advisors discuss his plan to tour the kingdom and heal the hurts caused by the war.\n4\tTalk to Thalhír in the Tower of Ecthelion\tThalhír, the Warden of Laws, is in the Tower of Ecthelion and has been called to answer whether the Heirs of Castamir remain a threat to the peace of Gondor.\n5\tListen to the discussion of the Heirs of Castamir\tKing Elessar and his advisors discuss his plan to tour the kingdom and heal the hurts caused by the war.\n6\tTalk to Queen Arwen in the Tower of Ecthelion\tQueen Arwen is in the Tower of Ecthelion and wishes to speak with you about a special task.\n7\tTalk to King Elessar in the Tower of Ecthelion\tKing Elessar is in the Tower of Ecthelion, waiting to hear if you will agree to this new plan.\n",
[6729]="70040538\n1\tSpeak with Hebil\tHebil stands over Fuirion in the middle of the corsairs' encampment. You should speak with Hebil.\n2\tTry to reason with Hebil\tHebil stands over Fuirion in the middle of the corsairs' encampment.\n3\tDefend yourself against the attacking Corsairs\tDefend yourself against the attacking Corsairs.\n4\tSpeak with Gladion\tGladion is at the Corsair encampment in northern Lamedon. You should speak with Gladion.\n",
[6730]="7002C4DE\n1\tSee what Gadda plans to do\tGadda stands with you in the Mead Hall of Stangard. You should speak with Gadda.\n2\tAddress your observations to Stanric when he is ready to hear you\tStanric is in the Mead Hall. You should speak with Stanric about what you saw in Stangard.\n3\tAddress your observations to Stanric when he is ready to hear you\tStanric is in the Mead Hall. You should speak with Stanric about what you saw in Stangard.\n4\tObserve the leaders' discussion\tYou should observe the discussion between the leaders of Stangard.\n5\tTalk to Sithric\tSithric is in the Mead Hall of Stangard.\n6\tWatch the discussion\tWatch the discussion in the Mead Hall.\n7\tTalk to Sithric\tSithric is in the Mead Hall at Stangard.\n8\tWait until Sithric is gone, then speak with Stanric\tStanric is in the Mead Hall at Stangard.\n9\tTalk to Stanric\tStanric is in the Mead Hall at Stangard.\n",
[6731]="70061C06\n1\tTalk to Boromir and hear what he has to say about Gondor\tIn June, Boromir and his brother Faramir were called by their father, the Steward of Gondor, to the White Tower.\n2\tListen to Boromir's tale\tDenethor, the Steward of Gondor, wrestles with many difficulties.\n3\tTalk to Boromir and hear what he has to say about the quest\tBoromir continues the tale of his journey.\n4\tTalk to Boromir and hear what he has to say about Rohan\tBoromir continues the tale of his journey.\n5\tConsider Gríma Wormtongue\030Consider Háma, Doorward of Théoden\030Consider Théodred, heir of Théoden\030Consider Éowyn, Lady of Rohan\030Consider Éomer, Marshal of the Mark\tThough he was denied an audience with Théoden, Boromir spoke with several members of his court.\n6\tTalk to Boromir and hear what he has to say about his journey\tBoromir continues the tale of his journey.\n7\tTalk to Boromir and hear what he has to say about the journey\tBoromir continues the tale of his journey.\n8\tListen to Boromir's tale of his journey\tSomeone unexpected left his home to speak with Boromir near the Gap of Rohan.\n9\tTalk to Boromir and hear what he has to say about the rest of the journey\tBoromir continues the tale of his journey.\n",
[6732]="7000011E\n1\tTalk to Isferon\tIsferon is standing inside the cave. Isferon is waiting to speak with you before he opens up the three boxes and learns what secrets his friend Berenin left behind when he sailed into the West.\n2\tWatch Isferon open the boxes and learn their secrets\tIsferon is standing inside the cave. Isferon is opening the boxes left to him by Berenin.\n3\tTalk to Isferon\tIsferon is standing inside the cave. Isferon has opened the three boxes his friend Berenin left behind when he sailed into the West.\n",
[6733]="70044291\n1\tTalk to Mithrandir in the Old Archives\tMithrandir is in the Old Archives of Minas Tirith.\n2\tTalk to Mithrandir in the Old Archives\tMithrandir is inside the Old Archives.\n3\tUse Scrolls\tMithrandir has asked you to search one of the chambers in the Old Archives for mention of Eärnur, the last King of Gondor.\n4\tShow the Eärnur scroll to Mithrandir in the Old Archives\tYou have found a scroll bearing Eärnur's name in many locations, and should show it to Mithrandir.\n5\tTalk to Mithrandir in the Old Archives\tMithrandir is in the Old Archives.\n6\tMithrandir has asked you to search another of the chambers in the Old Archives for mention of Eärnur, the last King of Gondor.\t\n7\tShow the book you found to Mithrandir in the Old Archives\tYou have found a book detailing the lineage of the Kings and the Stewards of Gondor, and should show it to Mithrandir.\n8\tListen to Mithrandir in the Old Archives\tMithrandir is in the Old Archives, and he bears a worried expression.\n9\tTalk to Mithrandir in the Old Archives\tMithrandir is in the Old Archives.\n",
[6734]="70047B5C\n1\tApproach the table\tYou should approach the table, where the four hobbits have already begun.\n2\tTalk to Pippin\tPippin wishes to speak to you.\n3\tEat or drink\030Enjoy the hobbits' company\tYou should join in the meal and partake of the food and drink laid out on the table.\n4\tTalk to Sam\030Enjoy the hobbits' company\tYou should hear what Sam says for himself.\n5\tEat or drink some more (total: 2)\030Enjoy the hobbits' company\tYou should help yourself to some more food and drink while the four friends talk.\n6\tTalk to Merry\030Enjoy the hobbits' company\tHear Merry's reply to Frodo.\n7\tTalk to Frodo\030Enjoy the hobbits' company\tListen to Frodo's answer to the complaint.\n8\tEat or drink some more (total: 3)\030Enjoy the hobbits' company\tYou should help yourself to some more food and drink while the four friends talk.\n9\tTalk to Pippin\030Enjoy the hobbits' company\tYou should hear what Pippin says to Frodo.\n",
[6735]="7006EAE1\n1\tLearn the severity of Corudan's injuries\tSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.\n2\tFollow Sigileth's account of her return from the Fearwater\tSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.\n3\tHear what Cúridwan had to say about Corudan's injuries\tSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.\n4\tShiver at the thought of the unnatural cold\tSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.\n5\tHear what Cúridwan had to say of the unnatural chill\tSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.\n6\tHear what Sigileth believed of the spirit\tSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.\n7\tHail the spirit, if spirit it be\tSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.\n8\tListen to Sigileth's account\tSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.\n9\tListen to Sigileth's account\tSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.\n10\tListen to Sigileth's account\tSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.\n11\tAsk Sigileth what she believes happened\tSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.\n12\tHear the remainder of Sigileth's account\tSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.\n13\tHear what Corudan had to say\tSigileth describes her return from the Fearwater with her brother and Cúridwan.\n",
[6736]="70059A6D\n1\tTalk to Venko\tVenko and Imák are ready to join the fight!\n2\tHear Thettmárr's dying words\tThettmárr has suffered grievous injury at the hands of the attacking Orcs, and will not long survive.\n3\tTalk to Imák\tImák knows there is no time to spend on grief.\n4\tTalk to Prince Ingór\tPrince Ingór requests your help in the middle of the battle.\n5\tRemain on your guard\tGorgar has emerged from the ranks of the Orcs to challenge the dwarves for control of Gundabad!\n6\tTalk to Stóthkell\tStóthkell has been grievously wounded by the mithril hammer wielded by Gorgar the Ruthless, and will not long survive.\n",
[6737]="70000121\n1\tTalk to Leigh Putnam\tLeigh Putnam is just inside the entrance of the cave. You have travelled with Leigh to the cave where refugees are seeking shelter from Orc-attacks.\n2\tTalk to Ford Beecher\030Talk to Gail Beecher\030Talk to Lind Newell\tThe refugees are hiding in the back of the cave. Leigh Putnam has asked you to try and lift the spirits of the refugees hiding in the cave and to convince them to come to Trestlebridge.\n3\tTalk to Severin Wheeler\tSeverin Wheeler has arrived in the cave with grim tidings. You have tried to convince the refugees to come to the relative safety of Trestlebridge, but they refused.\n4\tTalk to Leigh Putnam\tLeigh Putnam is inside the refugee cave. You have aided in the defence of the refugees, and now Leigh wishes to speak with you.\n",
[6738]="70037DB8\n1\tAragorn is atop the Deeping Wall, and wishes to speak with you.\t\n2\tGather worried defenders and send them to Aragorn atop the wall (total: 8)\tWorried defenders can be found atop the wall, and Aragorn has asked you to send them to him for encouraging words.\n3\tTalk to Aragorn\tAragorn stands atop the wall, ready to speak to the worried defenders.\n4\tHelp Aragorn to bolster the spirits of the defenders on the wall\tThe men of Rohan need inspiring words if they are to stand against Saruman's forces.\n5\tTalk to Thurketel atop the wall\tThurketel stands atop the wall. Did Aragorn's words help him recover his hope?\n",
[6739]="7006C6F1\n1\tApproach Raphûz's fire\tRaphûz is waiting for you to speak with him.\n2\tSit with Raphûz\030Listen to Rapûz's story\tRaphûz made his way to the fireside and invited you to sit.\n3\tShare a smoke with Raphûz\030Wait for the conversation to end\tRaphûz invited you to partake in his smoking device. Perhaps you should smoke your own pipe.\n4\tLaugh with Raphûz\030Wait for the conversation to end\tRaphûz finished his statement with a hearty laugh. You should laugh with him.\n5\tTalk with the woman and tell her why you are here\030Wait for the conversation to end\tA woman emerged from the shadows. She speaks with confidence and asks why so many from the north travel into Shagâna.\n6\tClear your throat to prompt Raphûz to respond with /ahem\030Wait for Ashâmi to take her leave\tThe woman introduced herself as Ashâmi. She asked for the deer. Raphûz appears stunned see if you can make him respond.\n7\tSpeak with Raphûz to get his reaction\tAshâmi left the fireside with the deer in tow. Raphûz watches her recede into the night.\n",
[6740]="7004C38A\n1\tTalk to Bingo by the camp-fire\tBingo is standing near the camp-fire on the edge of the Greenfields with his many cousins.\n2\tBingo's many cousins have scary stories to share, and you should choose one of them to begin.\t\n3\tListen to spooky stories with the Boffins\tThe dancing flames of the camp-fire illumine the faces of the Boffins, and a spooky hush descends.\n4\tBingo's many cousins have scary stories to share, and you should choose who goes next.\t\n5\tListen to spooky stories with the Boffins\tThe dancing flames of the camp-fire illumine the faces of the Boffins, and a spooky hush descends.\n6\tTalk to Bingo and hear his spooky story\tBingo has a spooky story to share.\n7\tListen to spooky stories with the Boffins\tThe dancing flames of the camp-fire illumine the faces of the Boffins, and a spooky hush descends.\n8\tHelp Esmeralda remove the cursed shoes\tEsmeralda cannot stop dancing! Is it the magic of the shoes?\n9\tRemain alert for a cure to the cursed shoes\tWhat is happening? The story-telling has taken a frightful turn!\n10\tTalk to Bingo by the camp-fire\tBingo is by the camp-fire on the edge of the Greenfields.\n",
[6741]="700604A8\n1\tTalk to Ravaedron outside Fernbrake Cot\tRavaedron is outside Fernbrake Cot, the home of his friends the Stagshorns.\n2\tAccompany Ravaedron as he bids farewell\tStand with Ravaedron and provide him the comfort he needs as he bids farewell.\n3\tTalk to Maddoc Stagshorn\tMaddoc Stagshorn has welcomed you to Fernbrake Cot.\n4\tTalk to Glenys Stagshorn inside Fernbrake Cot\tGlenys Stagshorn has welcomed you inside her home.\n5\tVisit with the Stagshorns as Ravaedron bids farewell\tStand with Ravaedron and provide him the comfort he needs as he bids farewell.\n6\tTalk to Maddoc Stagshorn inside Fernbrake Cot\tThe air has grown chilly inside Fernbrake Cot. Maddoc Stagshorn motions for you to speak with him.\n",
[6742]="70071BC1\n1\tTalk to Faeron\tYou have travelled with Faeron to Gebarakór, the Ordâkhai open-pit mine. You should talk to Faeron.\n2\tMove closer to the Ordâkhai\tAnother group is arriving at Gebarakór. You should move closer to hear what they are saying.\n3\tObserve the conversation\tAnother group has arrived at Gebarakór. You should listen in on what they are saying.\n4\tLook for Kugâna among the workers\tYou witnessed the arrival of Ombátha, the leader of the Bokhóri, sorcerers with the ability to ensnare Men's will. You should look for Kugâna, Nabatínu's wife, among the assembled workers.\n",
[6743]="70047B35\n1\tTalk to Gandalf\tGandalf has led you to Bâr Thorenion in North Ithilien, cut into a high place above Cormallen. You should talk to Gandalf to hear more about Bâr Thorenion.\n2\tTalk to Merry\030Talk to Pippin\tGandalf has invited everyone to step in and see Bâr Thorenion. You should talk to Merry and Pippin and hear what they think of it all.\n3\tExplore the central courtyard\030Explore the side quarters\030Explore the north passage\030Explore the southern passage\030Explore the kitchens\tExplore Bâr Thorenion with Merry and Pippin.\n4\tTalk to Pippin\tTalk to Pippin in the central courtyard, now that you have all explored Bâr Thorenion.\n5\tCollect some straw (total: 3)\030Collect some plates (total: 5)\030Collect Ithilien Wine (total: 3)\030Collect provisions crates (total: 4)\030Collect some kind of light (quantity: see journal)\tHelp Pippin and Merry gather the things needed for a makeshift meal.\n6\tLay the things about the table\tYou should bring the things you collected to the table.\n7\tTalk to Pippin\tPippin and Merry have come running back with their own findings.\n8\tEnjoy the meal\tJoin Merry and Pippin in enjoying the makeshift meal.\n",
[6744]="7002C5B8\n1\tTalk to Odda\tOdda is waiting to speak with you inside the Stangard Mead Hall.\n2\tTalk to Stanric about the Uruk's fate\tStanric stands at the head of the Stangard mead hall. Stanric wishes to discuss the capture of Dargum, and decide an appropriate course of action.\n3\tTalk to Sithric about the Uruk's fate\tSithric stands beside Stanric in the Stangard Mead Hall. Sithric wishes to discuss the capture of the Uruk and respond to Stanric's judgement.\n4\tTalk to Gadda about the Uruk's fate\tGadda stands before Stanric and Sithric in the Mead Hall. Gadda wishes to discuss the result of Stanric and Sithric's council.\n",
[6745]="70052756\n1\tMake your way through the tunnel to the Skarháld throne room\tThe Dwarves of Skarháld are in danger! You must hurry through the escape tunnel carved behind the fortress if you are to reach them before it is too late!\n2\tTalk to Kámat in the throne room\tKámat has been seriously wounded and is near death.\n3\tHurry to the exit of the keep and you may still save some lives\tKarazgar has left the keep. If you hurry you might still be able to save some of the Dwarves of Skarháld.\n4\tFind and confront Karazgar\tKarazgar has cut a swath of destruction through the Dwarves of Skarháld, but you may still have a chance to stop him.\n5\tStand with Gandalf in defence of the Dwarves of Skarháld\tKarazgar has come to Skarháld in fulfilment of his second promise.\n6\tPick up the mask of Karazgar\tKarazgar has escaped, but he left his mask behind.\n7\tBring the mask of Karazgar to Gandalf\tGandalf awaits the mask of Karazgar.\n",
[6746]="7006C6EF\n1\tJoin Raphûz by the fire\tJoin Raphûz by the fire.\n2\tSit with Raphûz by the fire\tRaphûz offers a seat by the fire.\n3\tTell Raphûz you do not think him a fool with no\tContinue conversing with Raphûz.\n4\tSmoke with Raphûz's device\tRaphûz suggested you share his tobacco.\n5\tCough at Raphûz, alerting him to your difficulty with his device\tYou used Raphûz's hookah, but the experience is different than smoking with your pipe.\n6\tSmoke with Raphûz\tYou continue listening to Raphûz's story. You should share a smoke with him using your pipe.\n7\tConclude your discussion with Raphûz\030Bow to Raphûz and take your leave\tThe evening grows long. Perhaps it is time to retire.\n",
[6747]="70065EC2\n1\tOffer to help Limril with dinner\tLimril is in her home in Dínadab in northern Lamedon. You should offer to help Limril with dinner while she waits for Gladion.\n2\tGather dishes from the hutch\tThe hutch is in the corner. Gather dishes from the hutch, and set the table.\n3\tSet the table for six (total: 6)\tThe table is in Gladion and Limril's home. Gather dishes from the hutch, and set the table.\n4\tTalk to Limril\tLimril is in her home in Dínadab in northern Lamedon. You should see what else Limril needs.\n5\tWait for the meal to begin\tYou have helped prepare for dinner, and should now wait for the meal to begin.\n6\tTalk to Gladion\tOvercome with emotion, Limril has become upset and Gladion is concerned for her.\n7\tTalk to Limril\tOvercome with emotion, Limril has become upset and Gladion is concerned for her.\n",
[6748]="7002C612\n1\tShow Wynmar the ruins of Haldirith on the path ahead\tWynmar has followed you to Haldirith and stands beside you now. You should talk to Wynmar.\n2\tEscort Wynmar to Haldirith\tWynmar followed you to Haldirith and seeks a final word with Noriel. You should escort Wynmar to Haldirith.\n3\tTell Ninil why Wynmar begged to come\tNinil is outside of Haldirith, waiting to speak with you.\n4\tTell the Elves why you have brought a trespasser to the Elf-keep\tNoriel is at Haldirith.\n5\tTalk to Noriel\tNoriel is at Haldirith.\n6\tObserve the meeting of Wynmar and Noriel\tNoriel and Wynmar are at Haldirith.\n7\tTalk to Noriel\tNoriel is at Haldirith.\n",
[6749]="700266C5\n1\tDestroy the Gift of Gorothúl in Lumul-nar\tBróin believes that one of the relics Gorothúl left behind in Moria was given to the merrevail infesting the Mirror-halls of Lumul-nar and wants you to destroy it.\n2\tDefeat Ergoth\tDefeat Ergoth, the dark Morraval that was drawn to Gift of Gorothúl.\n",
[6750]="70037083\n1\tTalk to Agelwyn\tAgelwyn can be found in the refugees' hiding spot north of Marton. You should help Agelwyn to put aside her anxiety and begin to lead her people.\n2\tListen to Agelwyn\tAgelwyn can be found in the refugees' hiding spot north of Marton. You should help Agelwyn to put aside her anxiety and begin to lead her people.\n3\tSpeak with Agelwyn\tAgelwyn can be found in the refugees' hiding spot north of Marton. You should help Agelwyn to put aside her anxiety and begin to lead her people.\n4\tListen to Agelwyn\tAgelwyn can be found in the refugees' hiding spot north of Marton. You should help Agelwyn to put aside her anxiety and begin to lead her people.\n5\tSpeak with Agelwyn\tAgelwyn can be found in the refugees' hiding spot north of Marton. You should help Agelwyn to put aside her anxiety and begin to lead her people.\n6\tListen to Agelwyn\tAgelwyn can be found in the refugees' hiding spot north of Marton. You should help Agelwyn to put aside her anxiety and begin to lead her people.\n",
[6751]="70052784\n1\tApproach Karazgar and hear what he has to say\tKarazgar has confronted you at the Old Ford, but for the moment he has declared a truce. He wishes only to speak with you.\n2\tGive your response to Karazgar\tKarazgar has confronted you at the Old Ford, but for the moment he has declared a truce. He wishes only to speak with you. He waits for you to respond.\n3\tAsk Karazgar the questions you wish\tKarazgar has confronted you at the Old Ford, but for the moment he has declared a truce. He wishes only to speak with you. He has given you the chance to ask the questions you wish.\n4\tListen to what Karazgar has to say\tKarazgar has confronted you at the Old Ford, but for the moment he has declared a truce. He wishes only to speak with you.\n5\tGive Karazgar your response to his request\tKarazgar has made his request of you: he wants you to give him the Black Book of Mordor.\n6\tRemain on your guard\tRemain alert for the reaction of Karazgar, and stay on your guard.\n7\tWait for the newcomers to arrive\tKarazgar has fled from the new arrivals on the road.\n8\tTalk to Elrond on the road near the Old Ford\tElrond and much of his household have made the passage of the mountains.\n",
[6752]="70042C38\n1\tTalk to Bingo\tYou have left the road and now Bingo wants to set up a camp-site for the night.\n2\tCollect suitable tinder (total: 4)\tBingo has asked you to look for suitable tinder for building a fire.\n3\tBuild a camp-fire at the place Bingo has chosen\tBingo must have chosen a good place for you to build a fire by now.\n4\tTalk to Bingo by the camp-fire\tBingo is sitting by the fire you built in the Trollshaws, ready to turn in for the night.\n5\tBingo is asleep, but someone needs to stay awake and alert to any dangers. That someone is you!\t\n6\tTalk to Bingo by the camp-fire\tThe hours of the night have passed... eventfully... and now Bingo has finally stirred.\n",
})
